{"title": "Infected Bunker Spider", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"druid-infobox druid-container noexcerpt\" id=\"druid-container-1\"><div><div class=\"druid-title\">Infected Bunker Spider</div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div class=\"druid-main-image\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-labels druid-tabs\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-label druid-tab druid-toggleable druid-title-tab focused\" data-druid=\"1-1\" data-druid-tab-key=\"In-Game\">In-Game</div></div><a href=\"/wiki/File:Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Infected Bunker Spider.jpg\" src=\"/images/thumb/Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg/250px-Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg?3d7acd\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg/375px-Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg?3d7acd 1.5x, /images/thumb/Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg/500px-Infected_Bunker_Spider.jpg?3d7acd 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Information\">Information</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-VariantOf\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-VariantOf\">Variant Of</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-VariantOf druid-data-nonempty\">\nBunker Spider</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-InternalID\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-InternalID\">Internal ID</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-InternalID druid-data-nonempty\">\nInfectedSandSpider</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-MaxCount\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-MaxCount\">Max Count</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-MaxCount druid-data-nonempty\">\n1</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-PowerLevel\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-PowerLevel\">Power Level</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-PowerLevel druid-data-nonempty\">\n2</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-CauseofDeath\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-CauseofDeath\">Cause of Death</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-CauseofDeath druid-data-nonempty\">\nMauling, Stabbing</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-IsBodyRecoverable\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-IsBodyRecoverable\">Is Body Recoverable?</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-IsBodyRecoverable druid-data-nonempty\">\nYes</div></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Stats\">Stats</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Health\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Health\">Health</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Health druid-data-nonempty\">\n5</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Damage\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Damage\">Damage</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Damage druid-data-nonempty\">\n4 or 90</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-DoorSpeedMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-DoorSpeedMultiplier\">Door Speed Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-DoorSpeedMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.15</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-StunTimeMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-StunTimeMultiplier\">Stun Time Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-StunTimeMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n1</div></div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> is a hostile entity and variant of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Bunker_Spider\">Bunker Spider</a> added by <b>Wesley's Ememy Variants</b>. It is a large white spider with black markings and two spikes of white mold on its body.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Mechanics\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Mechanics\">&gt; Mechanics</span></h2>\n<p>Similar to a Bunker Spider, an <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> will initially attempt to create a nesting area by placing several webs in the surrounding area and will typically stop if it encounters a player until line of sight is broken. Once all the webs have been laid down, the <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> will find a spot to wait until one of its webs is triggered, a player walks underneath it, or it is attacked by a player. It will then pursue that player.\n</p><p>Players that come into contact with the <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> will take 90 damage. Additionally, the white mold spikes on the <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> rapidly deal 4 damage per hit to players on contact. Any player that dies to either attack will be cocooned and hung from the ceiling, although the <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> typically is encountered on the exterior and the body will instead be hung on thin air. Regardless, the body can only be recovered via the ship teleporter.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Spawn_Conditions\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Spawn_Conditions\">&gt; Spawn Conditions</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> only naturally spawns on <a href=\"/wiki/Vindict\" title=\"Vindict\"><b>Vindict</b></a>, having a 36.04% chance to spawn on the exterior during daytime and a 39.62% chance to spawn in the interior.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Major_Story_Spoilers\">Major Story Spoilers</span></h3>\n<p>The <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> can additionally spawn <span class=\"spoiler-content\" style=\"\"><span>immediately on the exterior of one or several moons depending on if players let <a href=\"/wiki/ResearcherxB\" title=\"ResearcherxB\"><b>ResearcherxB</b></a> crash or decide to overload it. If players let it crash onto <a href=\"/wiki/Trite\" title=\"Trite\"><b>Trite</b></a>, several <b>Infected Bunker Spiders</b> will spawn on the exterior at the start of the day every time players land on Trite afterward on that save file.</span></span>\n</p><p><span class=\"spoiler-content\" style=\"\"><span>If players instead decided to overload the ship, debris from the ship can fall onto the exteriors of several moons. A couple or few <b>Infected Bunker Spiders</b> will spawn on the exterior of the moon every time players land on it afterward on that save file. The moons currently known to have a chance for debris to fall onto their exteriors are <a href=\"/wiki/Carnate\" title=\"Carnate\"><b>Carnate</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Core\" title=\"Core\"><b>Core</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Crowd\" title=\"Crowd\"><b>Crowd</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dune\" title=\"Dune\"><b>Dune</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Glace\" title=\"Glace\"><b>Glace</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Heap\" title=\"Heap\"><b>Heap</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Hyve\" title=\"Hyve\"><b>Hyve</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Infernis\" title=\"Infernis\"><b>Infernis</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Junic\" title=\"Junic\"><b>Junic</b></a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Selector\" title=\"Selector\"><b>Selector</b></a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Utril\" title=\"Utril\"><b>Utril</b></a>.</span></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Bestiary_Entry\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Bestiary_Entry\">&gt; Bestiary Entry</span></h2>\n<p>Players will receive an entry about the white mold growing on the <b>Infected Bunker Spider</b> rather than the entity itself.\n</p>\n<table class=\"article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>White mold <span style=\"padding-left:0.5em;\">&#x2060;</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table style=\"border: 15px solid #8E8E83; font-size: 135%; font-family: Tomorrow; color: #01A801; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 25px; background-color: #151515;\">WHITE MOLD<br /><br /><br />Scientific name: Cretyrus-botaharum<br /><br /><br />This is a dangerous species of mold which thrives in bright areas. It is capable of growing in dark places but prefers not to, very rarely it be found in shadow or complete darkness.<br /><br /><br />The mold grows en masse and is able to spread across large surfaces with rapid succession. Additionally, on occasion it clusters up and grows spike-like formations which act as a way of detecting motion and a means to spread itself through direct infection of any poor creature which gets stung by it.<br /><br /><br />The spike-like formations are able to sense both heat and vibrations through the air. It knows what sort of creatures are easier to spread through and which are not. Those it deems not viable, it tries to scare off by shaking its spikes. However it will not hesitate to sting when the opportunity arises regardless of what steps on it.<br /><br /><br />Unlike most infections, this one does not try to kill or harm the host, instead it tries to adapt to its host and strengthen the skeleton or exoskeleton, making them bulkier and more violent as a faster method of spreading to other creatures through the addition of spikes growing out of the bones it has strengthened. Comparisons have been made with Rabies lyssavirus, a disease which similarly alters behaviour to become more violent as a means to spread.<br /><br /><br />The I.T.D.A. has investigated several infestations of this mold and deemed it not to be a critical level invasive species and has successfully cleared large patches of the mold.<br />They highly advise everyone to report any instances of the white mold appearing and avoid direct contact.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Audio\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Audio\">&gt; Audio</span></h2>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Audio\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>Sound\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Walking</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"8\" data-mwtitle=\"SpiderWalk.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SpiderWalk.mp3?f5fa77\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SpiderWalk.mp3/SpiderWalk.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Attacking</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"2\" data-mwtitle=\"SpiderAttack.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SpiderAttack.mp3?a689ed\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SpiderAttack.mp3/SpiderAttack.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Being Hit</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"1\" data-mwtitle=\"SpiderHit.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SpiderHit.mp3?b54983\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SpiderHit.mp3/SpiderHit.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Being Stunned</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"1\" data-mwtitle=\"StunSpider.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/StunSpider.mp3?2432b0\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/StunSpider.mp3/StunSpider.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dying</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"1\" data-mwtitle=\"SpiderDie.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SpiderDie.mp3?f891f5\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SpiderDie.mp3/SpiderDie.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Gallery\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Gallery\">&gt; Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"An Infected Bunker Spider on the exterior.\"><img alt=\"An Infected Bunker Spider on the exterior.\" src=\"/images/thumb/InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg/120px-InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg?3f5b1c\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg/180px-InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg?3f5b1c 1.5x, /images/thumb/InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg/240px-InfectedBunkerSpiderExterior.jpg?3f5b1c 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">An Infected Bunker Spider on the exterior.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"